---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="LaunchKit — ship your product site" description="A fast, static-first public website for your next SaaS.">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Static-first SaaS marketing</p>
    <h1>Make the public side of your product feel instant.</h1>
    <p class="lead">LaunchKit is the small, focused site template for a landing page, content, and SEO — without pulling in a dashboard or a complex auth flow.</p>
    <a class="button" href="/register/">Crear cuenta</a><a class="text-link" href="/login/">Ya tengo una cuenta</a>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="card"><h2>Fast by default</h2><p>Pages are pre-rendered to HTML and ship no framework runtime for static content.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h2>Content-ready</h2><p>Use the included blog and docs routes as a starting point for your own content model.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h2>Focused interactivity</h2><p>The contact form adds only a tiny script where the page needs it.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
